+There are two types of openEHR paths used in AQL queries: an _archetype path_, referring to a node within an archetype, and a _RM class attribute path_, pointing to an attribute of an openEHR Reference Model class. An RM class attribute path is resolved on the type of the data it reaches, which may be a subtype of the type its attribute declares (e.g. `c/composer/name`, where `composer` holds a `PARTY_IDENTIFIED`); where that data has no such attribute, the path yields `NULL`. These paths uses also _predicate expressions_ (see <<_predicates>>) enclosed by brackets (`[]`), to define criteria for coarse-grained and fine-grained data.
 
 
